// games/sonic4/test/poison/poison_tail_if_unit_fold.emp — POISON (see README).
//
// TARGETS: sigil's `[eq.cross-type]` refusal, on the operand shape this tree can
// actually reach — a value that EMP_PITFALLS §1's silent unit fold turned into
// `()`, compared against an int.
// EXPECTED FRAGMENT: the refusal's class tag, operator and operand kinds —
// "[eq.cross-type] `==` not defined for unit and int".
//
// WHAT THIS PINS, AND WHAT IT USED TO PIN. Until 2026-09-02 comptime `==` was
// TOTAL: `() == -16` answered FALSE, so the ensure below evaluated, fired, and
// this case matched its own interpolated "TAIL_IF_UNIT_FOLD: ... folded P[0] to
// ()" text. Sigil then made equality refuse across comparison classes rather
// than answer a constant (merge 6a8b3ecd09e80b9e6e1d5751f61d07b3362e7aed,
// reachable from sigil origin/master; sigil docs/EMP_PITFALLS_EQUALITY.md §12 at
// that revision is the reference — it covers both operand orders, the two
// cross-kind comparisons that stay DEFINED, and why the unit lead is phrased as
// a lead and not a verdict). So the old claim this header made — that `() ==
// int` compares FALSE rather than erroring, and that a value ensure is
// therefore the engine's catch surface — is now FALSE in both halves: the
// compiler refuses first and the ensure below never evaluates at all. The catch
// surface moved EARLIER and got stronger; this fixture moved with it.
//
// Background (triangle-fold parcel, 2026-08-26): `deform_triangle`'s original
// body ended its `comptime for` element in a block-tail `if`/`else`, which sigil
// folds to `()` for EVERY input with NO diagnostic (EMP_PITFALLS §1, measured
// here even though the `if` is not nested). tail_if_tri() below is a verbatim
// copy of that PRE-FIX generator body, so `P` is a real folded-`()` array rather
// than a hand-written `unit` — this case reaches the refusal by the same road a
// regression would.
//
// WHY THIS IS KEPT RATHER THAN RETIRED — the reason it still exists. Cross-type
// equality can regress in two directions and they are NOT symmetric:
//   - regressed to comparing FALSE: the deform_triangle guards in
//     engine/level/parallax_dsl.emp fire with their own messages and the build
//     goes red anyway. Nothing is lost, and this case goes red too (the fragment
//     below stops matching), so it costs nothing to keep.
//   - regressed to comparing TRUE: EVERY one of those guards PASSES and a unit
//     fold ships silently. A guard that passes produces no artifact, so nothing
//     else in this tree can report it. THIS CASE IS THE TRIPWIRE ON THAT
//     DIRECTION, and it catches it on the COUNT (see below), not the fragment.
// It is deliberately the SECOND line — the primary detector for a sigil
// regression belongs in sigil's own suite — and its whole value is that it is an
// INDEPENDENT instrument: different tree, different mechanism, firing during our
// build.
//
// THE COUNT IS HALF THE ASSERTION. The lane row expects exactly 1 [Error]:
//   - today: `P[0]` is `()`, `F[0]` is -16, the comparison REFUSES — 1 diagnostic.
//   - if sigil ever fixes block-tail-if folding, `P[0]` becomes -16, the ensure
//     is int-vs-int, it PASSES, this module builds CLEAN, and the lane fails
//     THIS case on 0 errors — the signal that §1's trap is gone and this poison
//     (plus the pitfall entry) should be RETIRED, not that something broke.
//   - if the refusal regressed to answering FALSE, the ensure fires with the
//     message below — still 1 [Error], but the fragment no longer matches, so
//     the lane reports wording drift and sends a reader here.
// So 1-vs-0 separates "the refusal is working" from "the fold was really fixed",
// and the fragment separates "refused" from "answered".
//
// Zero bytes, ensures-only — unreachable from any real entry like every module
// in this directory; evaluated only by tools/emp_expect_fail.py.
module games.sonic4.test.poison.poison_tail_if_unit_fold

// Verbatim pre-fix deform_triangle body: the element expression is an if/else
// in block-tail position of the `comptime for` body — §1's shape.
comptime fn tail_if_tri(amplitude: int, period: int) -> [i8; 256] {
    return comptime for i in 0..256 {
        if (i % period) < (period / 2) {
            (((i % period) * amplitude * 4) / period) - amplitude
        } else {
            amplitude - ((((i % period) - period / 2) * amplitude * 4) / period)
        }
    }
}

const P = tail_if_tri(amplitude: 16, period: 64)
const F = deform_triangle(amplitude: 16, period: 64)

// ⚠ THE OPERAND ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING — DO NOT WRITE THIS AS `F[0] == P[0]`.
// The lane row's fragment pins `not defined for unit and int`, and sigil emits the
// two kinds in SOURCE ORDER: `eq_compatible(a, b)` reports `(desc(a), desc(b))`,
// lhs first, with NO normalisation — no sorting, no canonical order, no swap for
// readability (sigil's own source, read by that lane 2026-09-02; they pin both
// orders in their tests and will not silently normalise). So swapping these
// operands — a meaning-preserving edit any reader might make without thinking —
// flips the message to `int and unit`, the row goes red, and the failure points at
// the REFUSAL rather than at the swap that caused it. The unit side stays LEFT.
// This note sits here, at the edit site, and not only in the header, because the
// header is not where that edit gets made.
//
// This message is expected NEVER TO RENDER: the comparison is `unit == int`, and
// sigil refuses it before the ensure evaluates. It is written for the one world
// in which it DOES render — a refusal that regressed to answering false — which
// is why it describes that world rather than claiming to be the catch surface.
ensure(P[0] == F[0],
       "TAIL_IF_UNIT_FOLD: this text rendering AT ALL means comptime `==` answered instead of refusing — P[0] folded to {P[0]}, the shipped generator folds {F[0]}. Expected today: sigil's [eq.cross-type] refusal fires at the comparison and this ensure never evaluates. If P[0] just became a number, sigil fixed the fold and this poison should be RETIRED, see header")
